    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion, mini.snippets\n\n### Question\n\nI use mini.completion with mini.snippets and whenever I type a space the completion menu with snippets pops up. Is there a way to prevent this and to only have snippets be completed after a non-space character is typed?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.completion, mini.snippets</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I use mini.completion with mini.snippets and whenever I type a space the completion menu with snippets pops up. Is there a way to prevent this and to only have snippets be completed after a non-space character is typed?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.completion, mini.snippets\nQuestion\nI use mini.completion with mini.snippets and whenever I type a space the completion menu with snippets pops up. Is there a way to prevent this and to only have snippets be completed after a non-space character is typed?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2026-05-28T10:49:50Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This doesn't happen with most types of configuration. For example, it doesn't happen for me in Lua filetypes.\r\n\r\nThe common workflow is that the completion window is automatically shown after typing keyword character or a LSP completion trigger character. My guess is that there is a configuration that adds space (i.e. `\" \"`) as a completion trigger character. Could you please execute the following command that will print the capabilities of the active LSP server: `:lua vim.fn.append('.', vim.split(vim.inspect(vim.lsp.get_clients({buf = 0})), '\\n'))`. Then look for all instances of `server_capabilities.completionProvider.triggerCharacters` field (there will probably be several) and see which characters are present there.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This doesn't happen with most types of configuration. For example, it doesn't happen for me in Lua filetypes.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The common workflow is that the completion window is automatically shown after typing keyword character or a LSP completion trigger character. My guess is that there is a configuration that adds space (i.e. <code class=\"notranslate\">\" \"</code>) as a completion trigger character. Could you please execute the following command that will print the capabilities of the active LSP server: <code class=\"notranslate\">:lua vim.fn.append('.', vim.split(vim.inspect(vim.lsp.get_clients({buf = 0})), '\\n'))</code>. Then look for all instances of <code class=\"notranslate\">server_capabilities.completionProvider.triggerCharacters</code> field (there will probably be several) and see which characters are present there.</p>",
            "bodyText": "This doesn't happen with most types of configuration. For example, it doesn't happen for me in Lua filetypes.\nThe common workflow is that the completion window is automatically shown after typing keyword character or a LSP completion trigger character. My guess is that there is a configuration that adds space (i.e. \" \") as a completion trigger character. Could you please execute the following command that will print the capabilities of the active LSP server: :lua vim.fn.append('.', vim.split(vim.inspect(vim.lsp.get_clients({buf = 0})), '\\n')). Then look for all instances of server_capabilities.completionProvider.triggerCharacters field (there will probably be several) and see which characters are present there.",
